# Line endings: LF in the working tree, on every platform.
#
# This repo compares generated files BYTE-FOR-BYTE — a managed region must be a
# fixpoint of its own writer, and "a held block comes back identical" is a
# self-checked invariant. With core.autocrlf=true (the Windows default) git
# rewrites the working tree to CRLF on checkout, so every generated spec would
# stop matching the bytes the pipeline writes and the diff would churn on every
# run while nothing about the test changed.
#
# This overrides autocrlf, so the working tree matches what the tooling produces.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Real binaries — never normalised.
*.pptx binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
